      "title": "ElizaOS Discord Community Activity - July 8, 2026",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "A developer named mackroute announced a new plugin for Eliza agents designed to assess Solana token rug pull and honeypot risk before an agent executes a trade. The plugin returns a signed verdict with a score from 0 to 100 along with machine-readable reasons that can be verified offline. It operates on a pay-per-call model using USDC via x402, allowing agents to settle payments autonomously without requiring an account. A free lookup is available to test the model. The developer posted in the coders channel seeking feedback from developers who are actively running trading agents on Solana, specifically asking whether pre-trade risk checks would be useful or if they already handle risk assessment through other means.",
          "sources": [
            "https://discord.com/channels/1253563208833433701/1300025221834739744"
          ],
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "posters": [
            "https://cdn.elizaos.news/posters/1783561564841-d2a98j.jpg"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In the partners channel, community members exchanged casual greetings. One member expressed missing the group, which received positive reactions. Another member responded warmly, and a third tagged Shaw in a follow-up reply. Separately, in the general discussion channel, a message was flagged as spam by a community member in response to what appeared to be an airdrop announcement account.",
